---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: "Home", href: "/" },
  { name: "Terms & Conditions" },
];
---

<Base
  title="Terms & Conditions — RepMaths"
  description="Terms and conditions for using RepMaths free fitness, strength, and nutrition calculators."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
    <p>Last updated: September 13, 2026</p>

    <p>
      These Terms &amp; Conditions ("Terms") govern your access to and use
      of the RepMaths website and its calculators. By using RepMaths, you
      agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the
      website.
    </p>

    <h2>Use of the Website</h2>

    <p>
      RepMaths provides free, browser-based fitness, strength, nutrition,
      and body-composition calculators for personal, non-commercial use.
      You may use the calculators and content on this site for personal
      informational purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Permitted Use</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>
        You may use RepMaths calculators for personal fitness, training,
        nutrition, and educational purposes.
      </li>
      <li>
        You may share links to RepMaths pages with others.
      </li>
      <li>
        You may reference RepMaths results in personal notes, training
        logs, or similar personal records.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Prohibited Use</h2>

    <p>You agree not to:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        Copy, reproduce, scrape, or redistribute substantial portions of
        RepMaths content, calculator logic, or design without permission.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use automated tools to access RepMaths in a way that places
        unreasonable load on the website or its infrastructure.
      </li>
      <li>
        Attempt to reverse-engineer, modify, or interfere with the
        website's operation or security.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use RepMaths for commercial purposes, resale, or as part of a
        competing product without written permission.
      </li>
      <li>
        Represent RepMaths content or results as your own original work.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>

    <p>
      All content on RepMaths — including calculator logic, formula
      descriptions, design, layout, text, and branding — is the property
      of RepMaths unless otherwise stated. The underlying formulas used
      by RepMaths calculators are established, published methods from
      the fitness and sports-nutrition literature; see our
      <a href="/about/">About page</a> for details.
    </p>

    <p>
      You may not copy, redistribute, or republish RepMaths content
      without prior written permission.
    </p>

    <h2>No Professional Advice</h2>

    <p>
      RepMaths calculators and content are provided for informational and
      educational purposes only. They are not medical, nutritional, or
      fitness advice. See our
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> for important limitations
      and safety information.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>

    <p>
      RepMaths may use third-party services for analytics, advertising,
      hosting, security, and other website functionality. These services
      are governed by their own terms and privacy policies. See our
      <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details about
      third-party data handling.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>

    <p>
      RepMaths is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties
      of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to
      warranties of accuracy, reliability, merchantability, fitness for
      a particular purpose, or non-infringement.
    </p>

    <p>
      While RepMaths uses established formulas and methods, results are
      estimates and may not be accurate for every individual or situation.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>

    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, RepMaths and its
      operators will not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental,
      consequential, or special damages arising from or related to your
      use of the website, its calculators, or its content.
    </p>

